#: ../../c-api/pyexpat.rst:4
msgid "Expat C API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../c-api/pyexpat.rst:6
msgid ""
"The :mod:`xml.parsers.expat` module exposes selected Expat functions through "
"its ``expat_CAPI`` capsule. This allows extension modules to use the same "
"Expat library as Python. The interface is declared in :file:`pyexpat.h`, "
"which must be included after Expat's :file:`expat.h` header."
msgstr ""

#: ../../c-api/pyexpat.rst:13
msgid ""
"The name of the capsule containing the Expat C API: ``\"pyexpat."
"expat_CAPI\"``. Pass this to :c:func:`PyCapsule_Import` to obtain a pointer "
"to a :c:struct:`PyExpat_CAPI`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../c-api/pyexpat.rst:20
msgid ""
"The string identifying the layout of :c:struct:`PyExpat_CAPI`. Before using "
"the function pointers in the structure, check that its ``magic`` member "
"compares equal to this string using ``strcmp()`` and  its ``size`` member is "
"at least :c:expr:`sizeof(struct PyExpat_CAPI)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../c-api/pyexpat.rst:28
msgid ""
"Table of function pointers exported by :mod:`xml.parsers.expat`. The capsule "
"owns this structure: treat it as read-only and do not free it. Keep a strong "
"reference to the capsule while using the table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../c-api/pyexpat.rst:32
msgid ""
"Check the compatibility fields as described under :c:macro:"
"`PyExpat_CAPI_MAGIC` before using the function pointers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../c-api/pyexpat.rst:37
msgid "Interface identifier, set to :c:macro:`PyExpat_CAPI_MAGIC`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../c-api/pyexpat.rst:41
msgid ""
"Size of the structure in bytes, set to ``sizeof(struct PyExpat_CAPI)`` by "
"the :mod:`xml.parsers.expat` module that created the capsule."
msgstr ""

#: ../../c-api/pyexpat.rst:48
msgid ""
"Major, minor, and micro version numbers of the Expat library used by :mod:"
"`xml.parsers.expat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../c-api/pyexpat.rst:53
msgid ""
"Pointer to `XML_SetUnknownEncodingHandler <https://libexpat.github.io/doc/"
"api/latest/#XML_SetUnknownEncodingHandler>`_. The handler may set a Python "
"exception on failure. The caller must check for a Python exception after "
"parsing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../c-api/pyexpat.rst:60
msgid ""
"Python's unknown-encoding handler for Expat, used with "
"``XML_SetUnknownEncodingHandler``. It uses Python's codec registry to fill "
"*info*. The *encodingHandlerData* argument is unused. Calling this handler "
"requires an :term:`attached thread state`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../c-api/pyexpat.rst:66
msgid ""
"Pointers to the corresponding Expat functions, or ``NULL`` if not available "
"in the Expat version used by :mod:`xml.parsers.expat`, are listed below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../c-api/pyexpat.rst:70
msgid ""
"Member names omit the ``XML_`` prefix; for example, ``SetHashSalt`` exposes "
"Expat's ``XML_SetHashSalt`` function. See the `Expat API reference <https://"
"libexpat.github.io/doc/api/latest/>`_ for their behavior and the minimum "
"Expat version they appear in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../c-api/pyexpat.rst:99
msgid ""
"See the `Expat API reference <https://libexpat.github.io/doc/api/latest/>`_."
msgstr ""
